{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310770,"nonce":"kD96AwPNnLHywpSku4fzIZmBHdo=","title":"@:isVar SHIPPED: a property with backing storage now gets a field slot, and an accessor reading/writing its own property hits the slot ...","message":"`@:isVar` was **unimplemented** — `grep -rn 'isVar' compiler/src/` found only a\ndoc string. Two coupled defects; neither works alone.\n\n\nAll four sites that assign field indices skipped any property whose getter is\nnot `Default`. `field_index += 1` sits **after** the `continue`\n(`decl/metadata.rs:185`), which is why granting a slot shifts every later field.\n\nThe fix is `PropertyAccessInfo::has_backing_storage()` (`tast/node.rs`) with\n**all four callers routed through it**, so the layouts cannot drift:\n\n- `ir/mir/decl/metadata.rs:117` — primary (field_index_map, `record_class_field`,\n  struct definition)\n- `ir/mir/decl/metadata.rs:607` — derive codegen\n- `ir/mir/helpers/classes.rs:184` — `collect_parent_instance_fields`\n- `ir/mir/helpers/classes.rs:238` — `add_parent_fields`\n\nMissing even one puts a subclass's inherited fields at different offsets from\nthe parent's — silent overlap, the `bugs_stdtypes_type_addition_breaks_nue`\nfailure mode.\n\n**The marker rides in `PropertyAccessInfo`, deliberately NOT `SymbolFlags`.**\n`TypedField` carries no metadata, so SymbolFlags is the other available route —\nbut BLADE-restored field symbols get only STATIC (`compilation.rs:2371-2383`)\nwhile `BladeProperty` still restores getter/setter, so the flag could be absent\nin a context where `property_access` survived. Keeping the bit inside the struct\nthe predicate already reads makes that desync structurally impossible.\n\n**`BLADE_VERSION` 2 -\u003e 3 is mandatory.** `BladeCachedMaps` caches\n`(class_name, field_name, field_index)` and `class_sizes` and restores them\nverbatim (`compilation.rs:4505`, `:4536`); `compiler_version` is\n`CARGO_PKG_VERSION` and does not move between builds, so only this bump rejects\na stale cache. Skipping it is silent heap corruption. `.bsym` is NOT a second\nhazard — `BladeFieldInfo` carries no index and no size.\n\n`has_backing_storage()` is **narrower than Haxe's real rule**, which also counts\na `default`/`null` SETTER: `var x(get, null)` is physical in Haxe and gets no\nslot here (9 such properties in haxe-std). Widening it moves the instance layout\nof every class holding one — a layout change, not a comment fix.\n\n\nThere was no accessor-recursion guard. `is_inside_own_accessor()`\n(`field/access.rs`) is used by both dispatch sites (`field/access.rs`,\n`field/lvalue.rs`) and declines the accessor only when **the receiver register\nis the `this` register AND the function being lowered is that accessor** —\nHaxe's rule exactly. Verified against the oracle in both directions: another\nmethod of the same class still calls the accessor, and `other.name` inside\n`get_name` still calls it (`getCalls: 2`).\n\nEach guarded `Method(...)` arm needs a trailing `Method(_)` companion or the\nmatch is non-exhaustive.\n\n**Not `@:isVar`-specific.** `var v(default, set)` whose `set_v` writes `v`\nstack-overflowed at HEAD on plain Haxe the oracle prints `v: 42` for.\n\n\nFull harness, and note **the run has flakes**: two identical-binary runs of the\nsame build differed on `Issue3635` (CRASH -\u003e PASS) and `Issue4675`\n(WRONG_ANSWER -\u003e CRASH). Against the clean run: **431 PASS, zero gained, zero\nlost** — net-neutral, with two cases improved short of passing:\n\n- `Issue6375`: CRASH (stack overflow) -\u003e WRONG_ANSWER\n- `Issue9770`: COMPILE_FAIL (internal `index not found for write`) -\u003e WRONG_ANSWER\n\n`Xml`'s 8 `index not found for write` errors are gone and `Xml` compiles.\n`Xml.parse` still fails, now on a **different** blocker: `haxe.xml.Parser` hits\n`E0801 ambiguous dynamic method dispatch: exists` at `Parser.hx:366`\n(`escapes.exists(s)`) — the Map/structural-dispatch family, not this work.\n\n\nHaxe's `ctx.curfield` stays the accessor inside a lambda, so\n`rollback = () -\u003e memberField = 3` **writes the slot directly**. rayzor's guard\nuses `builder.current_function()`, which is the lambda, so it dispatches to the\nsetter: oracle `3`, rayzor `1`. Fixing it needs BOTH:\n\n1. an enclosing-accessor context that survives `lower_lambda_body`\n   (`expr/lambda.rs:245` clears `symbol_map`), and\n2. a way to recognise the **captured** `this` — MIR shows the receiver is a load\n   chain out of the closure env (`$12 = load *void $11`), not\n   `symbol_map[SymbolId(0)]`.\n\nBlast radius of the whole change is tiny: `@:isVar` appears on exactly two\ndeclarations in all of haxe-std, both in `Xml` (`Xml.hx:135` `nodeName`,\n`:140` `nodeValue`); layout goes 1..4 -\u003e 1..6, alloc 32 -\u003e 56. No currently\npassing program's layout moves.\n\nRelated: [[bugs-assignment-rereads-its-target]] (found while verifying this —\nit is why accessor-count probes disagree with the oracle),\n[[bugs-abstract-properties-need-setter-writeback]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `feature_isvar_backing_storage` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}